[17592186395121 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that if $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ and ${\\sigma }_{i}\\ne 0,$ then the $i$th column of $U$ can be found as\n\n$$\n{u}_{i}=\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{i}}A{v}_{i},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${v}_{i}$ is the $i$th column of the matrix $V.$\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=10$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=7.$ Therefore, the first column of $U$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{40}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395122 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395122 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395122 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395122 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395122 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395122 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395122 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395122 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186395126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395122 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "af024373-62e6-5fa0-a940-575a299d6f21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395123 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395123 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395123 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5dd82220-ad9a-5d23-9059-b9e91a7e8ddf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395124 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sq